1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,577
Mastery evidence. You have learned the Linux administration toolkit. Now you prove it.

2
00:00:06,127 --> 00:00:08,949
Mastery means someone else could check your work.

3
00:00:08,949 --> 00:00:10,734
So this lesson gives you a lab,

4
00:00:10,734 --> 00:00:12,635
a checker that says pass or fail,

5
00:00:12,635 --> 00:00:14,938
and a report that shows how you thought.

6
00:00:15,488 --> 00:00:19,648
I will build the lab, fix the first fault live, and leave the other three to you.

7
00:00:21,698 --> 00:00:23,319
Meet the tidy shop server.

8
00:00:23,319 --> 00:00:24,753
It has a report script,

9
00:00:24,753 --> 00:00:25,501
a data disk,

10
00:00:25,501 --> 00:00:26,374
a web service,

11
00:00:26,374 --> 00:00:27,309
and a firewall.

12
00:00:27,859 --> 00:00:32,936
Four things are broken, on purpose. A checker prints pass or fail for four checks.

13
00:00:33,486 --> 00:00:35,299
One: the report script runs.

14
00:00:35,849 --> 00:00:37,897
Two: the data disk accepts a write.

15
00:00:38,447 --> 00:00:40,879
Three: the service file verifies clean.

16
00:00:41,429 --> 00:00:44,309
Four: the shop page answers on port 8080.

17
00:00:44,859 --> 00:00:48,209
Your mission: four pass lines, with proof for every fix.

18
00:00:50,259 --> 00:00:54,462
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

19
00:00:55,012 --> 00:01:00,686
The repository is github dot com, slash it dash waves, slash devops dash A I.

20
00:01:01,236 --> 00:01:03,674
The lab is one file: lab36.sh,

21
00:01:03,674 --> 00:01:06,275
in the academy slash lab folder.

22
00:01:06,275 --> 00:01:11,882
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson36.

23
00:01:12,432 --> 00:01:14,357
Install it in three steps.

24
00:01:14,357 --> 00:01:15,913
Clone the repository.

25
00:01:15,913 --> 00:01:17,468
Go to the lab folder.

26
00:01:17,468 --> 00:01:21,690
Install the script into slash usr slash local slash sbin.

27
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,262
Three commands run everything.

28
00:01:24,262 --> 00:01:26,081
Lab up builds the problems.

29
00:01:26,081 --> 00:01:28,709
Lab check prints pass or fail for each.

30
00:01:28,709 --> 00:01:30,326
Lab down removes it all.

31
00:01:30,876 --> 00:01:37,574
Lab is a short name. Source the shortcuts file, and it runs sudo lab36.sh for you.

32
00:01:38,124 --> 00:01:41,373
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root,

33
00:01:41,373 --> 00:01:42,311
python three,

34
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:42,961
iptables,

35
00:01:42,961 --> 00:01:43,322
curl,

36
00:01:43,322 --> 00:01:44,838
and system D analyze.

37
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:47,148
Run it only in your own machine.

38
00:01:49,498 --> 00:01:50,430
Now for real.

39
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:52,509
I have cloned the repository,

40
00:01:52,509 --> 00:01:55,734
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

41
00:01:55,734 --> 00:01:56,666
Type: cd lab.

42
00:01:57,216 --> 00:01:59,371
List what is here. Type: ls.

43
00:01:59,921 --> 00:02:04,139
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

44
00:02:04,139 --> 00:02:06,249
Install the script.

45
00:02:06,249 --> 00:02:12,022
Type: sudo install -m 755 lab36.sh /usr/local/sbin/.

46
00:02:12,022 --> 00:02:16,795
Dash m seven five five makes it executable.

47
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:22,017
Load the short names. Type: source shortcuts36.sh.

48
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:27,837
Build the lab. Type: lab up. It takes a few seconds, because it builds a small disk.

49
00:02:32,387 --> 00:02:34,968
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

50
00:02:36,518 --> 00:02:40,678
Four FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

51
00:02:42,728 --> 00:02:44,477
Keep four notes for every fault.

52
00:02:45,027 --> 00:02:47,993
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the error.

53
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,975
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

54
00:02:51,525 --> 00:02:53,807
Three: the fix. One change only.

55
00:02:54,357 --> 00:02:56,789
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

56
00:02:57,339 --> 00:02:59,494
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

57
00:03:01,544 --> 00:03:02,422
Fault one,

58
00:03:02,422 --> 00:03:02,861
live.

59
00:03:02,861 --> 00:03:07,074
The checker says the report script does not run.

60
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:09,882
Run it the way the checker does.

61
00:03:09,882 --> 00:03:13,832
Type the full path: /opt/lab36/bin/report.sh.

62
00:03:14,382 --> 00:03:15,255
Note one,

63
00:03:15,255 --> 00:03:18,260
the symptom: permission denied.

64
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:19,229
Now check,

65
00:03:19,229 --> 00:03:20,490
do not guess.

66
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:23,107
Type: ls -l /opt/lab36/bin.

67
00:03:23,657 --> 00:03:24,256
Note two,

68
00:03:24,256 --> 00:03:24,921
the cause.

69
00:03:24,921 --> 00:03:26,716
The mode has no x anywhere,

70
00:03:26,716 --> 00:03:28,777
so nobody may execute the file.

71
00:03:28,777 --> 00:03:30,505
This listing is the proof.

72
00:03:31,455 --> 00:03:36,469
Note three, one change. Type: chmod u+x and the same path.

73
00:03:37,019 --> 00:03:39,408
Note four, the proof. Run the script again.

74
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:43,030
It runs. Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

75
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,166
One PASS,

76
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:44,882
three FAIL.

77
00:03:44,882 --> 00:03:45,858
One fault down,

78
00:03:45,858 --> 00:03:46,575
one change,

79
00:03:46,575 --> 00:03:47,291
with proof.

80
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:49,895
Now it is your turn for the other three.

81
00:03:51,945 --> 00:03:55,721
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

82
00:03:56,271 --> 00:03:58,404
Setup: the checker output at the start.

83
00:03:58,954 --> 00:04:00,576
Each fault, with its four notes.

84
00:04:01,126 --> 00:04:04,283
The final checker output, all four lines saying pass.

85
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:05,961
Where you got stuck,

86
00:04:05,961 --> 00:04:07,146
and what unstuck you.

87
00:04:07,146 --> 00:04:09,910
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

88
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:12,530
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

89
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:17,531
Your three faults. No spoilers, only directions.

90
00:04:18,081 --> 00:04:21,297
Check two says the data disk will not accept a write.

91
00:04:21,297 --> 00:04:22,572
Read the exact error.

92
00:04:22,572 --> 00:04:24,635
Then recall how you measure space,

93
00:04:24,635 --> 00:04:25,910
and what is using it.

94
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:29,679
Check three says the service file does not verify.

95
00:04:29,679 --> 00:04:33,543
System D analyze will tell you in plain words what is wrong.

96
00:04:34,093 --> 00:04:36,949
Check four says the page does not answer.

97
00:04:36,949 --> 00:04:39,038
Is anything listening on 8080?

98
00:04:39,038 --> 00:04:39,526
If yes,

99
00:04:39,526 --> 00:04:41,407
ask what stands in the way.

100
00:04:41,407 --> 00:04:43,287
Look at the firewall rules.

101
00:04:43,837 --> 00:04:48,125
Same method every time. Symptom, check, fix one thing, verify.

102
00:04:50,175 --> 00:04:53,567
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

103
00:04:56,117 --> 00:04:59,147
Proof one: is any lab disk still mounted?

104
00:04:59,147 --> 00:05:00,034
Type: mount,

105
00:05:00,034 --> 00:05:00,403
pipe,

106
00:05:00,403 --> 00:05:01,733
grep dash c lab36,

107
00:05:01,733 --> 00:05:03,285
to count the matches.

108
00:05:03,835 --> 00:05:10,086
Zero. Proof two: is the web server gone? Type: pgrep -fc and the pattern, in quotes.

109
00:05:10,636 --> 00:05:11,107
Zero.

110
00:05:11,107 --> 00:05:14,781
Proof three: is the firewall rule gone?

111
00:05:14,781 --> 00:05:16,947
Type: sudo iptables -S,

112
00:05:16,947 --> 00:05:17,418
pipe,

113
00:05:17,418 --> 00:05:19,020
grep dash c 8080.

114
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:25,543
Zero. Proof four: is the folder gone? Type: ls /opt/lab36.

115
00:05:26,093 --> 00:05:27,732
No such file or directory.

116
00:05:27,732 --> 00:05:29,119
Everything is removed.

117
00:05:29,119 --> 00:05:31,704
Paste these four proofs into your report.

118
00:05:33,754 --> 00:05:37,679
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

119
00:05:38,229 --> 00:05:40,064
The checker shows four pass lines.

120
00:05:40,614 --> 00:05:43,814
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

121
00:05:44,364 --> 00:05:46,113
You changed one thing at a time.

122
00:05:46,663 --> 00:05:49,479
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

123
00:05:50,029 --> 00:05:52,376
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind.

124
00:05:52,926 --> 00:05:55,315
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

125
00:05:55,865 --> 00:05:57,487
To pass, you need all six.

126
00:05:59,537 --> 00:06:05,404
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

127
00:06:05,954 --> 00:06:08,727
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

128
00:06:09,277 --> 00:06:12,093
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

129
00:06:12,643 --> 00:06:15,864
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

130
00:06:16,414 --> 00:06:18,526
Four: write the report from the template.

131
00:06:19,076 --> 00:06:22,255
Five: run the checker. All four lines must say pass.

132
00:06:22,805 --> 00:06:24,768
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

133
00:06:25,318 --> 00:06:27,152
Pause the video, and begin now.

134
00:06:42,702 --> 00:06:43,577
Quick check.

135
00:06:44,127 --> 00:06:46,217
Which command counts what is still mounted?

136
00:06:46,767 --> 00:06:48,474
What are the four notes for a fault?

137
00:06:49,024 --> 00:06:51,883
How many changes do you make before you verify?

138
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:53,990
What proves your cleanup worked?

139
00:06:54,540 --> 00:07:02,775
Mastery evidence covered: M C zero four, building on objectives one to ten.

140
00:07:03,325 --> 00:07:05,394
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

141
00:07:15,944 --> 00:07:17,992
Next masterclass: Bash scripting.

142
00:07:18,542 --> 00:07:21,870
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
